{{$NEXT}}

    - Add [PruneCruft] to dist.ini so build artifacts (blib/,
      pm_to_blib, MYMETA.*) no longer leak into release tarballs.

    - Fix SIGKILL-stale-peer leak in the SharedMem clients map.  When
      a client died via SIGKILL (or segfault, OOM, parent-exit
      cascade -- anything bypassing Perl's DESTROY) its shared-memory
      registration persisted forever, so the next process trying to
      register with the same id croaked 'Client <id> already exists'.
      Three-pronged fix mirroring IPC::Manager's AI_DOCS plan for the
      same defect: (a) init() reaps the stale entry when the recorded
      pid is certain-dead (pid_is_running == 0) and proceeds with a
      fresh registration; (b) peer_left() is implemented as an
      opportunistic sweep of every dead-pid entry plus its messages
      and stats; (c) peers() filters dead-pid entries so peer_delta
      in IPC::Manager::Role::Service actually fires peer_left.
      Foreign-but-running pids and live local pids remain treated as
      legitimate collisions.

